1.Write a Java program to create a class called "Person" with a name and age attribute. Create two instances of the "Person" class, set their attributes using the constructor, and print their name and age.
******************************************************************************************

class person{
    int age;
    String name;
    person(int a,String n){
        age=a;
        name=n;
    }
    void personDetails(){
        System.out.printf("Person's NAME = %s %nPerson's AGE = %s %n",name,age);
    }
}
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {

		person p1=new person(20,"Ram Samy");
		person p2=new person(32,"Kattamuthu");
		p1.personDetails();
		p2.personDetails();
	}
}
